# Keep gitless `vercel deploy` uploads small and keep `vercel build` from
# recursing into build output / stale git worktrees. Without this, `vercel deploy`
# bundles the untracked sites/ (ICS scaffold, ~475MB) and the built public/
# (~350MB) and fails with "Request body too large. Limit: 10mb"; and function
# bundling follows data/** into .claude/worktrees/* copies and loops.
#
# NOTE: Vercel CLI deploys strip .git from the build env regardless of this file,
# so CLI deploys emit empty "Update history" (build-page-changelogs). Correct
# changelogs require the git-based build (Vercel Deploy Hook building origin/main
# from GitHub); keep .git excluded here since uploading it changes nothing.
#
# Everything here is build output, a separate project's tree, or local-only.
sites/
public/
node_modules/
raw/
.git/
.vercel/output/
.claude/
